          "statement": "Consider the permutations in $S_8$: $$\\sigma = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 2 & 3 & 4 & 5 & 6 & 7 & 8 \\\\ 3 & 5 & 7 & 8 & 1 & 6 & 4 & 2 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\tau = (1 \\; 4 \\; 7)(2 \\; 8)(3 \\; 6 \\; 5)$$ 1. Write $\\sigma$ as a product of disjoint cycles. 2. Compute the order $|\\sigma|$ and parity $\\text{sgn}(\\sigma)$. 3. Compute the product $\\sigma \\tau$ in disjoint cycle form, and determine if $\\sigma \\tau \\in A_8$.",
