          "title": "Classification of Groups of Order $p^2$ and the $G/Z(G)$ Theorem",
          "question": "1. Provide a rigorous, self-contained proof that if $G / Z(G)$ is cyclic, then $G$ is abelian. 2. Using this result along with Part 2 of the previous problem, classify all groups of order $p^2$ up to isomorphism, proving that any group of order $p^2$ is isomorphic to either $\\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ or $\\mathbb{Z}_p \\times \\mathbb{Z}_p$.",
          "statement": "1. Provide a rigorous, self-contained proof that if $G / Z(G)$ is cyclic, then $G$ is abelian. 2. Using this result along with Part 2 of the previous problem, classify all groups of order $p^2$ up to isomorphism, proving that any group of order $p^2$ is isomorphic to either $\\mathbb{Z}_{p^2}$ or $\\mathbb{Z}_p \\times \\mathbb{Z}_p$.",
